    "title": "Man sought by Lexington police for alleged organized criminal ties - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Corey Elam ,\n10 hours ago\nLEXINGTON, Ky. ( FOX 56 ) — Lexington officials announced on Wednesday that a search was underway for a suspect with alleged involvement in organized crime.\nLATEST KENTUCKY NEWS: The Lexington Police Department (LPD) announced on April 8 that 19-year-old Denis Villanueva-Gutierez. He has a warrant issued for first-degree wanton endangerment, discharge of a firearm, and engaging in organized crime.\nDenis Villanueva, 19, has a warrant for his arrest, alleging he was involved in organized crime. (Bluegrass Crime Stoppers) Anyone with information that could help police find Villanueva-Gutierez is asked to call the Lexington Police Department at (859) 258-3600. Anonymous tips can be submitted to Bluegrass Crime Stoppers by calling (859) 253-2020, visiti ng bluegrasscrimestoppers.com , or through the P3 Tips app, available at p3tips.com .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 56 News.\n2",
